    "created_at": "2022-03-31T21:27:51Z",
    "updated_at": "2022-03-31T21:27:51Z",
    "body": "I think `display: block` on `script` and `style` is more of a hack. I don't see why we should encourage it. Content should be marked up as content.\r\n\r\nIn particular, the content would not be accessible in non-CSS user agents. Search engines would likely skip it as not-content.\r\n\r\nThe correct way to mark up scripts and style sheets intended to be read by the user is `<pre><code>`.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
